Answers:

1. Berlin is the capital city of Germany. It is significant in German history as it was divided into East and West during the Cold War era, symbolizing the Cold War division of the world into two blocks. The fall of the Berlin Wall in 1989 marked the end of this division.
2. Germany shares borders with the following countries: Denmark, Poland, Czech Republic, Austria, Switzerland, France, Luxembourg, Belgium, and the Netherlands. Any three of these countries would be correct.
