5. Germany consists of a temperate seasonal climate, with moderate to heavy rainfall throughout the year. The climate varies based on geographic location and altitude. In the North, Germany has a maritime influenced climate with warmer summers and milder winters, while the South has a more continental influenced climate with hotter summers and colder winters.
